Syntax: plate <item>

Plate builds a piece of armor up a tier: clothing becomes light, light
medium, medium heavy.  It offers more protection and fewer people can wear
it, which is the whole of the bargain.

Two things limit it.  Material hardness caps how far anything can climb --
silk will never be plate, whatever your skill -- so a mage's transmutation
is what opens the ladder above soft stock.  And what a smith can install is
capped by the skill ceiling: a piece already finer than that keeps what it
has and merely changes tier.

The material is checked when you start and again when you finish, since a
mage may transmute the piece while you work.

See also: STRIP, TRANSMUTE, BOLSTER, FORGE
